{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a3e479dc92ff23b0","name":"Immobilizer 418 Interdictor-Class Heavy Cruiser","source":{"id":"source:reference-a3e479dc92ff23b0","title":"Immobilizer 418 Interdictor-Class Heavy Cruiser","revision":18720,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:37:08Z","sha256":"1d1bcbf6631a67f4a48b2e74300ec8112f430fec6773c66873b3ec7964fc8a01","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18720","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Immobilizer%20418%20Interdictor-Class%20Heavy%20Cruiser&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a3e479dc92ff23b0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Immobilizer 418 ",{"tag":"i","children":["Interdictor"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," used to pull ships out of hyperspace and prevent them from reentering, trapping them in realspace and keeping them from escaping. The Immobilizer 418 uses four massive gravity well generators that produce a gravity shadow in hyperspace (similar to that projected by a planet or star) that makes hyperspace travel through that area impossible. When an Immobilizer 418 has its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gravity Well Projectors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gravity_Well_Projectors"}," fired up, any ships traveling through hyperspace in the vicinity immediately revert to realspace, and no ship within a hyperspace interdiction area can make the jump to lightspeed until the gravity well generators are shut down.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Immobilizer 418 was developed in response to the hit-and-run tactics of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"},". The success of the Immobilizer 418 once again gave the Empire an advantage over Rebel tacticians, though fortunately for the Alliance, only a relatively small number of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Interdictor"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers were converted for use during the Galactic Civil War. However, the ships were so successful that some ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Destroyers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Destroyers"}," were retrofitted with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gravity Well Projectors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gravity_Well_Projectors"}," in order to provide a more powerful platform for interdiction technology.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The Immobilizer 418 is typically accompanied by a contingent of more heavily armed vessels, not only to lie in ambush but also to protect the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Interdictor"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser from the ships they are trapping. Pulling a Rebel fleet out of hyperspace typically makes the Immobilizer 418 the primary target of the trapped fleet, and as a result the ship needs protection in order to keep from being destroyed.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Once the Immobilizer 418 has pulled the targets from hyperspace, the ship's crew must keep the gravity wells focused on the trapped fleet; otherwise their prey will escape into hyperspace simply by outrunning the Immobilizer and its fellow ships. Directing a gravity well is no simple matter, requiring the same kind of precision and expertise as is required to operate a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beam"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beam","referenceId":"reference:627f44a03c76e65b"},", and the Immobilizer 418's crew is specially trained to maintain gravity wells in the heat of combat.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Immobilizer 418 ",{"tag":"i","children":["Interdictor"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser Statistics (CL 17)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Cruiser) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 52; +15 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 1,500; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 20; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"},": 150; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 252\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Fly 2 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},")\n"]},{"